--
Was KNOWNBUG: std::make_tuple at arity >= 3 returned a nondeterministic
tuple (make_tuple's body conversion failed and was swallowed as a
system-header body).  Arity <= 2 passed via the tuple<_T1,_T2> partial
specialization.

ROOT (fixed, 2026-07-15, two layers): (1) N5008 [temp.variadic]/8 -- the
in-class parameter-pack replication replaced the pattern `const _Elements&`
wholesale with the raw pack element, dropping the const, so tuple's
converting constructor `tuple(const _Elements&...)` could not bind the
three rvalue arguments ([dcl.init.ref]/5) and vanished from the overload
set (see cpp11_const_pack_pattern_param for the minimal header-free case).
(2) N5008 [basic.scope.temp] -- template_mapt::lookup_by_suffix preferred a
nil placeholder binding of a sibling partial specialization's same-named
parameter (__strip_reference_wrapper's primary-vs-spec `_Tp`) over the
bound parameter of the enclosing alias instantiation, aborting
__decay_and_strip<_Elements>::__type elaboration; nil entries are now
skipped (they are not live bindings).
